   "text": "I read the image as a cyclic peptide and wrote the SMILES residue by residue.\n\n**Residues and connectivity**\n- **Asp:** the free N-terminal amine sits on the Asp \u03b1-carbon. Its side-chain carbonyl forms an amide with the Lys \u03b5-nitrogen, which closes the ring.\n- **Asn:** the Asp backbone C=O is bonded to the Asn NH. The Asn side chain is CH2C(=O)NH2.\n- **Ile:** the Asn C=O is bonded to the Ile NH, and the Ile C=O is bonded to the proline nitrogen.\n- **Proline:** it carries a 1,2,3-triazol-1-yl group at C4. The triazole bears a 4-(thiophen-2-yl)phenyl group at its own C4 position.\n- **Benzothienylalanine:** the proline C=O is bonded to its NH. Its side chain is a CH2 attached to benzothiophen-3-yl.\n- **Lys:** the Bta C=O is bonded to the Lys \u03b1-NH. Lys ends in a primary carboxamide (C(N)=O) and has a four-CH2 side chain leading to the ring-closing amide.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI assigned each wedge or hash from the drawing using CIP priorities.\n- Asp \u03b1, Asn \u03b1, Ile \u03b1, Lys \u03b1 and Pro C2 all come out as the natural L (S) configuration. I assumed Asn and Bta are L, as the drawing leaves them ambiguous.\n- Ile C\u03b2 is S, so the side chain is L-isoleucine, not allo.\n- Pro C4 is S, from the wedge to the triazole nitrogen.\n\nSMILES: N[C@H]1CC(=O)NCCCC[C@@H](C(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2csc3ccccc23)NC(=O)[C@@H]4C[C@H](n5cc(-c6ccc(-c7cccs7)cc6)nn5)CN4C(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)CC)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC1=O"
